Reversed Array: 5 4 3 2 1
```

In this implementation, we use two indices `start` and `end` to traverse the array from both ends. We swap the elements at these indices until `start` becomes greater than or equal to `end`, effectively reversing the order of the elements in the array. The time complexity of this implementation is O(n) as we need to iterate over each element once, where n is the number of elements in the array.

